a big announcement today from the city  of north las vegas there's a new  commercial development center coming to  the downtown area it's going to be  located at north 5th street and lake  mead boulevard jeremy j ford showing us  what's in store for surrounding  communities  tuesday morning city leaders made an  announcement to develop 19 acres of land  into a gateway commercial plaza ward one  councilman isaac baran says the nlv  gateway is a total reinvestment in the  downtown area it's been years and coming  this is not something that's like been  something we just we just dreamed up of  it actually has taken many years to put  all the pieces in place a previous  administration  developed the downtown redevelopment  agency to do just this you know to  self-fund a transformation in the  downtown core the specific tenets have  not yet been announced but are expected  to include national retailers medical  groups and spaces for entrepreneurs a  groundbreaking is expected within the  next two months with the completion of  the project expected by 2024. jeremy j  ford live local now
 

